T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> Example 1.3: Transformer Efficiency & Annual Carbon Offset Calculation) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Statement: A 100 MVA, 400/132 kV, 3-phase grid step-down transformer has an iron core) Tj
T*
(loss \(no-load loss\) of P_i = 45 kW and full-load copper loss of P_cu = 180 kW.) Tj
T*
(\(a\) Determine the transformer efficiency at full load operating at 0.85 power factor) Tj
T*
(lagging.) Tj
T*
(\(b\) Determine the load kVA at which maximum efficiency occurs, and calculate the maximum) Tj
T*
(efficiency.) Tj
T*
(\(c\) An older transformer had P_i = 90 kW and P_cu = 320 kW. Calculate the annual energy) Tj
T*
(saved \(kWh\) by the modern transformer operating 24 hours/day, 365 days/year at an) Tj
T*
(average load factor of 75%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Step-by-Step Solution:) Tj
T*
(1. Full Load Efficiency at cos\(Phi\) = 0.85:) Tj
T*
(- Active Output Power: P_out = S * cos\(Phi\) = 100,000 kVA * 0.85 = 85,000 kW) Tj
T*
(- Total Losses: P_loss = P_i + P_cu = 45 kW + 180 kW = 225 kW) Tj
T*
(- Input Power: P_in = P_out + P_loss = 85,000 + 225 = 85,225 kW) Tj
T*
(- Efficiency eta = \(P_out / P_in\) * 100 = \(85,000 / 85,225\) * 100 = 99.736%) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Load for Maximum Efficiency \(x_max\):) Tj
T*
(- Maximum efficiency occurs when variable copper loss equals constant iron loss: x^2 *) Tj
T*
(P_cu = P_i) Tj
T*
(- Fraction of full load: x_max = sqrt\(P_i / P_cu\) = sqrt\(45 / 180\) = sqrt\(0.25\) = 0.50) Tj
T*
(\(i.e., 50% load\)) Tj
T*
ET

