(3. Annual Energy Savings Comparison:) Tj
T*
(- Operating hours per year: T = 24 * 365 = 8,760 hours.) Tj
T*
(- Average load fraction: x = 0.75 \(75% load\).) Tj
T*
(- Loss of Modern Transformer: P_loss_mod = 45 + \(0.75\)^2 * 180 = 45 + \(0.5625 * 180\) =) Tj
T*
(45 + 101.25 = 146.25 kW) Tj
T*
(- Loss of Older Transformer: P_loss_old = 90 + \(0.75\)^2 * 320 = 90 + \(0.5625 * 320\) = 90) Tj
T*
(+ 180 = 270.00 kW) Tj
T*
(- Power saved: Delta_P = 270.00 - 146.25 = 123.75 kW) Tj
T*
(- Annual Energy Saved = 123.75 kW * 8,760 h = 1,084,050 kWh \(over 1.08 Million) Tj
T*
(Units/year\)!) Tj
T*
